  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Nightshelf merchant and Orca Incursion survivor, resident of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ — a Nightshelf colony carved from the Berg's deep tunnels — where he was elevated during the Clever Ice Age for reasons the ice-memory records more clearly than any living account. His hands still shake when fire-braziers flicker too low. His left flipper bears a frostburn scar curving like a question mark from wrist to knuckle; the Incursion gave him that, though he has never specified which moment.
    
    Valveus-morb~ trades in goods that should not cross the colonial boundary: aurora-crystal shards moved downward, fire-core fragments moved upward, and silences sold to anyone who can afford them. He was nominally employed by The Cell (owl-sworn), the Nightshelf merchant guild that once controlled the volcanic trade routes through ☽'slew Ravium~. In practice, his loyalty ran to Glow-Trader Vaulius-phantasm~, the only penguin who knew him before the raids and the only one he reportedly never lied to about what he witnessed in the deep.
    
    The Cell has since posted a bounty of four fire-cores for his capture alongside Vaulius-phantasm~, charging both with violations of the Pactum∴silenti — diverting glacial passages, selling unauthorized aurora-crystals from unsurveyed depths, and extracting material from sanctified ground near the Glow-Fissure. His whereabouts are unknown.
    
    ## The Omega Obelisk Descent
    
    Valveus-morb~ carried an unpaid debt to Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss, the Nightshelf founder who died beneath Terrace Momiou. That debt drove him to accompany ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~, the outlawed Communion teacher, into the deep tunnels when the Omega Obelisk began its ascent. The artifact's pressure-dreams forced his Incursion memories to the surface. Its coral tendrils reached for him before ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~'s sealing broke its hold. Valveus-morb~ contributed his own witness to the binding — speaking aloud the names of penguins he had watched die, names he had never spoken before.
    
    He is recorded as a practitioner of the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, Shawl☽ Sun, and Star∴eternal. He refuses to look directly at aurora-light. The chronicle sources do not explain why, and I will not speculate where they declined to.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771579548298_0", anchor: "a bounty of four fire-cores for his capture", text: "Four. The Rofundis∴rupt has collapsed ☽'scar Ramtatus~'s primary vein. The Profun∴lapsum flooded Wane☽ Oncea's deep mines. The Cell lost ☽'slew Ravium~ to the Midnight Claws and by every measure is hemorrhaging capital. Four fire-cores is not a bounty. It is a budget line that someone approved knowing full well what four fire-cores costs a waning guild during a supply crisis. Either Valveus-morb~ took something from the Glow-Fissure worth more than the bounty, or The Cell is spending resources it does not have to recover something it cannot admit wanting.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579548298_1", anchor: "the only one he reportedly never lied to", text: "\"Reportedly.\" A merchant who trades in silences. Whose colleagues cannot verify his honesty because his honesty is definitionally invisible to them. Who reports this — Vaulius-phantasm~? The man himself? The source is either the liar or the person the liar claims to exempt.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771579548298_2", anchor: "extracting material from sanctified ground near the Glow-Fissure", text: "Every guard posted to the Glow-Fissure rotates out at seventy-two hours because the Fissure makes sustained proximity intolerable. The sanctification perimeter exists precisely because the corruption there consumes ice-memory. Whatever Valveus-morb~ extracted, he extracted it from ground that eats records. The Pactum∴silenti charges are convenient. Desecration of a corruption site is a serious offense that requires no further explanation — which makes it the ideal charge when the actual offense requires too much.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579548298_3", anchor: "a practitioner of the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, Shawl☽ Sun, and Star∴eternal", text: "One scatters the caster's memories. One hollows them. One never lets them sleep. A trauma survivor who flinches at dimming fire has made himself proficient in three disciplines whose cumulative cost is the systematic destruction of the self. This is not a skill portfolio. It is a inventory of ways to disappear while still standing upright.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
